+## 3. End-to-end workflows
+
+### 3.1 Organising the work: one insertion
+
+```
+INPUT: strategy S, graph G (n nodes), decision step D, meter E, new_name x
+
+1. assert E is MeteredEmbedder
+2. assert S._embedder is None or S._embedder is E
+3. assert x is a valid bare name and x not in G
+4. t0 <- now()
+   shortlist <- S.shortlist(x)
+   t1 <- now()
+5. validate shortlist: tuple, no x, no duplicates, all in G,
+   scores length matches candidates
+6. if shortlist empty:
+       outcome <- (edges=(), calls=0, seconds=0)
+       decide_s <- 0
+   else:
+       t2 <- now()
+       outcome <- D.decide(x, shortlist.candidates, G.domain_context)
+       t3 <- now(); decide_s <- t3 - t2
+7. validate edges: tuple, no duplicates, 2-tuples of str, no self-loop,
+   every edge involves x, other endpoint in shortlist
+8. t4 <- now()
+   G.add_node(x)
+   for (p, d) in outcome.edges: G.add_prereq_edge(p, d)
+   apply_s <- now() - t4
+9. record meter before update
+   t5 <- now(); S.on_inserted(x, outcome.edges); t6 <- now()
+   update_s <- t6 - t5
+   embedding_calls_in_update <- meter.calls delta
+   embed_in_update_s <- meter.seconds delta
+10. total_s <- shortlist_s + decide_s + apply_s + update_s
+    validate_s <- shortlist-validation seconds + edge-validation seconds
+11. diagnostics <- S.diagnostics() or {"diagnostics_error": repr(e)}
+12. return InsertionResult(...)
+```
+
+### 3.2 Accuracy mode (leave-one-out)
+
+```
+INPUT: HarnessConfig(mode="accuracy"), strategy factory, decision step,
+       embedder factory, corpora {DSA, Metacademy}
+
+1. require confirm=True unless dry_run
+2. create output dir; write manifest.json
+3. optional warmup (CLI uses it to write strategy_config.json once)
+4. if resume: load successful keys (and failed keys unless retry_failed)
+5. planned keys <- for each corpus, each sampled held-out node, each repeat
+   - DSA: all 29 nodes
+   - Metacademy: deterministic sample of min(30, 141) nodes
+6. for each corpus, repeat, held-out node h:
+       if key skipped: continue
+       if max_llm_calls reached: write summary; return
+       G' <- gold graph with h removed
+       S <- fresh strategy from factory
+       E <- MeteredEmbedder(fresh embedder)
+       S.setup(G', E)                 # untimed
+       gc.collect()
+       snapshot LLM meter before
+       t0 <- now()
+       result <- insert_node(S, G', D, h, metered_embedder=E)
+       wall <- now() - t0
+       snapshot LLM meter after; delta = after - before
+       score <- score_node_insertion(h, gold graph, judgments,
+                                     result.shortlist.candidates, result.edges)
+       append success record to raw.jsonl (flush)
+   on setup error: append failed record, write summary, abort
+   on LLMTransportError: append failed record; abort only if fail_fast
+   on any other error: append failed record, write summary, abort
+7. regenerate summary.csv
+```
+
+### 3.3 Sweep mode (cost-only scaling)
+
+```
+INPUT: HarnessConfig(mode="sweep"), name pool, strategy, decision step
+
+1. require confirm=True unless dry_run
+2. write manifest
+3. for each size n in sweep_sizes, each trial t in 0..trials-1:
+       seed <- config.seed + n*1000 + t
+       sample n+1 unique names from pool
+       existing <- first n; new_name <- last
+       G <- names-only ConceptGraph(domain_context="computer science")
+       S <- fresh strategy; E <- MeteredEmbedder(fresh embedder)
+       S.setup(G, E)
+       gc.collect()
+       result <- insert_node(S, G, D, new_name, metered_embedder=E)
+       append success/failed record with metrics + LLM snapshot delta
+4. regenerate summary.csv
+```
+
+### 3.4 CLI decision flow (`scripts/run_experiment.py main`)
+
+```
+parse args
+  └─ resolve strategy factory from STRATEGY_FACTORIES
+  └─ reject inapplicable flags (e.g. --theta on brute_force) -> exit 2
+  └─ instantiate probe strategy (no setup) -> catches bad params
+  └─ if --live and strategy uses embeddings and --embedder fake: refuse
+  └─ derive default run id from (mode, strategy, config)
+  └─ build HarnessConfig
+  └─ inspect sidecar; if resuming into existing dir, require same
+     strategy/config/mode/embedder -> else exit 1
+  └─ choose corpora (DSA / Metacademy / both)
+  └─ if --live sweep and no --names-file: refuse
+  └─ compute planned-call upper bound (strategy-aware, resume-aware)
+  └─ if --live:
+        print pre-flight estimate (calls, duration, cost)
+        check peak window; refuse unless --allow-peak
+        if --dry-run: print and exit 0
+        require --confirm
+        build DeepSeekClient + MeteredLLMClient + PairwiseDecisionStep
+     else:
+        FakeLLMClient + MeteredLLMClient + PairwiseDecisionStep
+  └─ build sweep name source (validated --names-file or placeholders)
+  └─ if --dry-run: print plan, resolved dir, exit 0
+  └─ require --confirm
+  └─ build embedder factory:
+        no embeddings or --embedder fake -> FakeEmbedder(dim=32)
+        else -> MiniLMEmbedder(); pin_cpu_threads(1)
+  └─ build ProgressReporter; attach on_call hook
+  └─ warmup writes strategy_config.json sidecar if dir fresh
+  └─ run_experiment(...)
+```
+
+### 3.5 Analysis pipeline
+
+```
+run_analysis.py --results-dir R --output-dir O
+  └─ STEP 1 validate_all_runs(R)                  # fail-closed
+        if any run fails: print errors, exit 1, write nothing
+  └─ create O/tables, O/figures; write O/RUN_INFO.txt
+  └─ if --only posthoc:
+        build T1/T2 in memory
+        run_posthoc_stage(...)                     # T5–T9b, F7–F9
+        exit
+  └─ write T3 from validator CSV
+  └─ if accuracy runs: T1, T4; F4, F5, F6, F6b
+  └─ if sweep runs: T2 + slope fits; F1, F2, F3, F1b, F2b
+  └─ print success
+```
+
+### 3.6 Strategy lifecycle (normative; see `strategy-interface.md`)
+
+```
+construct strategy(config..., seed)
+    |
+    |  max_candidates(n_existing) may be called BEFORE setup
+    v
+setup(graph, embedder)          # untimed; graph read-only; may embed batch
+    |
+    v
+loop for each inserted node:
+    shortlist(new_name)         # timed; embeds once; caches vector
+    on_inserted(new_name, edges)# timed; reuses cache; never re-embeds
+```
+
