+### 4.2 `src/graph_insertion/graph_representation.py`
+
+**Purpose:** the in-memory domain model. Backing store is a NetworkX
+`DiGraph`; nodes are bare concept-name strings; an edge `(u, v)` means *u is
+a prerequisite of v* ([D-22], [D-23], [D-21]). Also stores the full pairwise
+gold judgment set, including explicit label-0 pairs and unjudged pairs.
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `SourceKind` | 29 | Enum | `GOLD`, `MEKG_EXAMPLE`; selects column-orientation mapping |
+| `oriented_edge` | 48 | function | label-1 file row -> canonical `(prereq, dependent)` |
+| `embed_text` | 91 | function | bare name -> embedding payload (underscores to spaces) |
+| `_validate_concept_name` | 113 | function | non-empty `str`, no `.txt` suffix |
+| `ConceptGraph` | 130 | dataclass | graph wrapper |
+| `ConceptGraph.add_node` | 158 | method | add node after validation |
+| `.has_node` | 163 | method | membership |
+| `.nodes` | 166 | method | node view |
+| `.num_nodes` | 170 | method | count |
+| `.add_prereq_edge` | 177 | method | add `prereq -> dependent`, rejects self-loop |
+| `.has_prereq_edge` | 190 | method | edge membership |
+| `.prerequisites_of` | 194 | method | in-neighbours |
+| `.dependents_of` | 198 | method | out-neighbours |
+| `.num_edges` | 202 | method | edge count |
+| `.edges` | 205 | method | edge view |
+| `.is_acyclic` | 213 | method | DAG check |
+| `.nx_graph` | 221 | property | raw `nx.DiGraph` (read-only by convention) |
+| `.copy` | 229 | method | independent deep copy |
+| `.without_node` | 240 | method | copy with one node and incident edges removed |
+| `_Label` | 271 | Enum | `ZERO=0`, `ONE=1`, `MISSING=-1` |
+| `GoldJudgmentSet` | 277 | dataclass | full pairwise judgment set |
+| `.record` | 308 | method | record `(col1,col2,label)`, reject conflicting duplicate |
+| `.get` | 339 | method | return `_Label`, default `MISSING` |
+| `.is_prerequisite` | 346 | method | `True` / `False` / `None` |
+| `.judgment_for_edge` | 357 | method | canonical-edge lookup via `oriented_edge` |
+| `.all_judged_pairs` | 382 | method | `(col1, col2, int_label)` list |
+| `.num_labeled_one` | 386 | method | count of label-1 pairs |
+| `.num_labeled_zero` | 389 | method | count of label-0 pairs |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+oriented_edge(kind, col1, col2):
+    if kind == GOLD:          return (col2, col1)   # D-15
+    if kind == MEKG_EXAMPLE:  return (col1, col2)   # D-19
+    raise ValueError
+
+embed_text(name):
+    return name.replace("_", " ")                   # D-21; no domain context
+
+_validate_concept_name(name):
+    if not str or empty: raise ValueError
+    if endswith(".txt"): raise ValueError            # D-16 / D-21
+
+ConceptGraph.add_node(name):
+    validate(name); _g.add_node(name)
+
+ConceptGraph.has_node(name): return _g.has_node(name)
+ConceptGraph.nodes():        return _g.nodes()
+ConceptGraph.num_nodes():    return _g.number_of_nodes()
+
+ConceptGraph.add_prereq_edge(prereq, dependent):
+    validate both; if prereq == dependent: raise ValueError
+    _g.add_edge(prereq, dependent)                   # auto-adds endpoints
+
+ConceptGraph.has_prereq_edge(p, d): return _g.has_edge(p, d)
+ConceptGraph.prerequisites_of(name): return list(_g.predecessors(name))
+ConceptGraph.dependents_of(name):    return list(_g.successors(name))
+ConceptGraph.num_edges():            return _g.number_of_edges()
+ConceptGraph.edges():                return _g.edges()
+ConceptGraph.is_acyclic():           return nx.is_directed_acyclic_graph(_g)
+
+ConceptGraph.copy():
+    return ConceptGraph(_g=_g.copy(), domain_context=domain_context)
+
+ConceptGraph.without_node(name):
+    validate(name)
+    if not has_node(name): raise KeyError
+    new <- copy(); new._g.remove_node(name); return new
+
+GoldJudgmentSet.record(col1, col2, label):
+    if label not in (0, 1): raise ValueError
+    if existing label for (col1,col2) exists and differs: raise ValueError
+    _judgments[(col1,col2)] <- _Label(label)
+
+GoldJudgmentSet.get(col1, col2):
+    return _judgments.get((col1,col2), MISSING)
+
+GoldJudgmentSet.is_prerequisite(col1, col2):
+    label <- get(col1,col2)
+    if MISSING: return None
+    return label == ONE
+
+GoldJudgmentSet.judgment_for_edge(prereq, dependent):
+    # invert the file-orientation mapping, then look up the file columns
+    col1, col2 <- oriented_edge(source_kind, prereq, dependent)
+    return is_prerequisite(col1, col2)
+
+all_judged_pairs():  return [(c1,c2,lbl.value) for each pair]
+num_labeled_one():   count labels == ONE
+num_labeled_zero():  count labels == ZERO
+```
+
+**Important detail.** `judgment_for_edge` applies `oriented_edge` in the
+*forward* direction to recover the file's column order. For GOLD,
+`oriented_edge(GOLD, prereq, dependent)` returns `(dependent, prereq)`, which
+is the original file order for a label-1 row. This lets scoring check both
+directions of a predicted edge without storing direction twice.
+
