+
+### 4.3 `src/graph_insertion/loader.py`
+
+**Purpose:** discover and strictly parse the 12 corpora into `ConceptGraph`
+and `GoldJudgmentSet`, applying the verified per-file conventions
+([D-15], [D-16], [D-19], [D-21], [D-23], [D-27]).
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `DEFAULT_DATASET_ROOT` | 26 | constant | `<repo>/repositories/dataset/EKG-Dataset` |
+| `CORPUS_DOMAIN_CONTEXT_MAP` | 31 | constant | exact corpus stem -> domain string |
+| `TAG_DOMAIN_CONTEXT_MAP` | 46 | constant | `DS` / `ML` / `logic` tag -> domain string |
+| `derive_domain_context` | 53 | function | stem or tagged filename -> domain or `None` |
+| `CorpusSpec` | 79 | frozen dataclass | name, path, source kind, context, delimiter, suffix flag |
+| `CorpusStats` | 107 | frozen dataclass | line/node/pair/duplicate/self-loop/positive counts |
+| `LoadedCorpus` | 120 | dataclass | graph + judgments + context + stats |
+| `discover_corpora` | 148 | function | exactly 12 specs in canonical order |
+| `_spec_from_path` | 228 | function | infer `CorpusSpec` from a path |
+| `load_corpus` | 254 | function | resolve target and parse |
+| `_parse_corpus_file` | 312 | function | strict line-by-line parser |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+derive_domain_context(filename_or_stem):
+    stem <- basename without extension
+    if stem in CORPUS_DOMAIN_CONTEXT_MAP: return map[stem]
+    tag <- first parenthesised substring of stem
+    if tag starts "DS":    return "data structures and algorithms"
+    if tag starts "ML":    return "machine learning"
+    if tag == "logic":     return "mathematical logic"
+    return None
+
+discover_corpora(root=None):
+    dir <- root or DEFAULT_DATASET_ROOT
+    require dir exists, DSA file exists, Metacademy file exists
+    examples <- sorted(glob("MEKG_with*.txt"))
+    require len(examples) == 10
+    specs <- [DSA spec (GOLD, ";", no suffix, DSA context),
+              Metacademy spec (GOLD, " ", no suffix, ML-math context)]
+    for p in examples:
+        specs.append(CorpusSpec(p.stem, p, MEKG_EXAMPLE,
+                                derive_domain_context(p.stem),
+                                delimiter=";", has_txt_suffix=True))
+    return specs                                 # order is stable
+
+_spec_from_path(path):
+    if "gold_standard" in stem:
+        kind <- GOLD; delimiter <- " " if "metacademy" else ";"; suffix <- False
+    else if stem starts "MEKG_with":
+        kind <- MEKG_EXAMPLE; delimiter <- ";"; suffix <- True
+    else:
+        kind <- GOLD; delimiter <- ";"; suffix <- False
+    return CorpusSpec(..., domain=derive_domain_context(stem))
+
+load_corpus(target, root=None):
+    if target is str:
+        if it names an existing file: spec <- _spec_from_path(path)
+        else:
+            specs <- discover_corpora(root)
+            match exact name, else case-insensitive exact, else substring
+            if none: ValueError; if ambiguous exact tie: ValueError
+    else if target is Path: spec <- _spec_from_path(target)
+    else if target is CorpusSpec: spec <- target
+    else: TypeError
+    return _parse_corpus_file(spec)
+
+_parse_corpus_file(spec):
+    require file exists
+    graph <- ConceptGraph(domain_context=spec.domain_context)
+    judgments <- GoldJudgmentSet(source_kind=spec.source_kind)
+    counters <- zeros; seen_nodes <- set(); distinct_pairs <- set()
+    for line_no, raw in enumerate(file, 1):
+        line <- strip(raw); if empty: continue
+        line_count += 1
+        parts <- split(line, spec.delimiter)
+        if len(parts) != 3: ValueError with file/line
+        label_str must be "0" or "1"; label <- int
+        if spec.has_txt_suffix:
+            both columns must end ".txt"; strip suffix
+        add each concept to graph on first appearance
+        if c1 == c2:
+            self_loop_rows += 1
+            if label == 1: ValueError
+        if pair seen: duplicate_rows += 1 else record pair
+        judgments.record(c1, c2, label)              # conflicting labels abort
+        if label == 1:
+            positive_row_count += 1
+            prereq, dependent <- oriented_edge(kind, c1, c2)
+            graph.add_prereq_edge(prereq, dependent)
+    stats <- counts from counters + graph.num_edges()
+    return LoadedCorpus(...)
+```
+
+**Delimiter warning.** Metacademy is space-delimited. Concept names in that
+file contain no spaces, so `split(" ")` is safe; this is verified in
+`data-formats.md`. DSA and all `MEKG_with*` files are semicolon-delimited.
+
