+### 4.6 `src/graph_insertion/embedding_minilm.py`
+
+**Purpose:** production embedding backend. Loads
+`sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` on CPU at a pinned revision, with
+fail-closed version checks.
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `SENTENCE_TRANSFORMERS_VERSION_PIN` | 30 | constant | `"6.1.0"` |
+| `MODEL_REVISION_PIN` | 33 | constant | HF commit hash |
+| `MODEL_NAME` | 35 | constant | `"all-MiniLM-L6-v2"` |
+| `MODEL_DIM` | 36 | constant | `384` |
+| `MiniLMEmbedder` | 41 | class | embedder implementation |
+| `.__init__` | 70 | method | pin checks, lazy import, version check, CPU model |
+| `.embed` | 114 | method | 1-D float32 `(384,)` |
+| `.embed_many` | 124 | method | 2-D float32 `(N, 384)` |
+| `.identity` | 138 | method | sidecar metadata |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+MiniLMEmbedder.__init__(revision=_UNSET):
+    require SENTENCE_TRANSFORMERS_VERSION_PIN is a non-blank str
+    actual_revision <- MODEL_REVISION_PIN if revision is _UNSET else revision
+    require actual_revision is a non-blank str
+    import sentence_transformers; import SentenceTransformer   # lazy
+    require installed __version__ == pin
+    model <- SentenceTransformer(MODEL_NAME, revision=actual_revision,
+                                 device="cpu")
+
+MiniLMEmbedder.embed(text):
+    arr <- float32(model.encode(text)).reshape(-1)
+    require arr.shape == (384,)
+    return arr
+
+MiniLMEmbedder.embed_many(texts):
+    if empty: return empty((0, 384), float32)
+    arr <- float32(model.encode(list(texts)))
+    if single text and 1-D: reshape(1, -1)
+    require arr.shape == (len(texts), 384)
+    return arr
+
+MiniLMEmbedder.identity():
+    return {model_name, dim, revision, sentence_transformers_version,
+            version_pin, device="cpu", dtype="float32"}
+```
+
+**Deliberate failure mode.** Any missing or mismatched pin raises rather than
+silently falling back. This protects cross-run comparability.
