+### 4.8 `src/graph_insertion/decision.py`
+
+**Purpose:** the shared final step. Exactly one LLM call per shortlisted
+candidate, sequential, strict token parsing, canonical edge construction
+([D-29], [D-23], [D-21]).
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `PROMPT_VERSION` | 26 | constant | `"v2"` |
+| `CALLS_PER_CANDIDATE` | 28 | constant | `1` |
+| `SYSTEM_PROMPT` | 30 | constant | prerequisite definition + 3 few-shot examples |
+| `VALID_TOKENS` | 42 | constant | `X_PREREQ_Y`, `Y_PREREQ_X`, `NONE` |
+| `parse_token` | 45 | function | strip/upper -> token or `None` |
+| `DecisionParseError` | 68 | exception | strict-mode parse failure |
+| `PairwiseDecisionStep` | 76 | class | `DecisionStep` implementation |
+| `.__init__` | 83 | method | store client + strict flag |
+| `.build_user_prompt` | 87 | method | optional subject line + two concepts |
+| `.decide` | 100 | method | loop over candidates |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+parse_token(text):
+    token <- upper(strip(text))
+    return token if token in VALID_TOKENS else None
+
+PairwiseDecisionStep.build_user_prompt(new_name, cand, domain_context):
+    x <- embed_text(new_name); y <- embed_text(cand)
+    if domain_context is not None:
+        return "Subject area: {domain}\nConcept X: {x}\nConcept Y: {y}"
+    return "Concept X: {x}\nConcept Y: {y}"
+
+PairwiseDecisionStep.decide(new_name, candidates, domain_context):
+    if candidates empty: return ((), 0, 0.0)
+    edges <- []; total_seconds <- 0
+    for cand in candidates:                      # strictly sequential
+        prompt <- build_user_prompt(new_name, cand, domain_context)
+        resp <- llm_client.complete(SYSTEM_PROMPT, prompt)
+        total_seconds += resp.latency_s
+        token <- parse_token(resp.text)
+        if token == X_PREREQ_Y: edges.append((new_name, cand))
+        elif token == Y_PREREQ_X: edges.append((cand, new_name))
+        elif token == NONE: pass
+        else:
+            if strict: raise DecisionParseError
+            if client has record_parse_failure: client.record_parse_failure(resp.text)
+    return DecisionOutcome(tuple(edges), len(candidates), total_seconds)
+```
+
+**Parse-failure policy.** Default is non-strict: an unparseable response
+produces no edge and is counted on the meter. `--strict` mode aborts. The
+official runs use the default.
+
