+### 4.9 `src/graph_insertion/llm.py`
+
+**Purpose:** LLM transport abstraction. `MeteredLLMClient` wraps any client
+and accounts calls, attempts, retries, latency, tokens, cache hits, model IDs,
+and parse failures. `DeepSeekClient` is the live OpenAI-compatible HTTP
+client with retry/backoff.
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `LLMTransportError` | 27 | exception | carries `attempts`, `retry_wait_s` |
+| `LLMResponse` | 46 | frozen dataclass | text + token/latency/model metadata |
+| `LLMSnapshot` | 85 | frozen dataclass | cumulative meter snapshot |
+| `.__sub__` | 105 | method | pointwise delta; parse-failure list suffix diff |
+| `LLMClient` | 133 | Protocol | `complete(system, user) -> LLMResponse` |
+| `MeteredLLMClient` | 146 | class | metering decorator |
+| `.set_on_call` | 176 | method | register heartbeat callback |
+| `._invoke_on_call` | 180 | method | call callback; count errors; warn once |
+| `.complete` | 192 | method | delegate + account success/failure |
+| `.record_parse_failure` | 227 | method | count and store raw text |
+| `.snapshot` | 232 | method | immutable snapshot |
+| `.reset` | 249 | method | zero all meters |
+| `resolve_model_alias` | 273 | function | explicit > env > `deepseek-flash` |
+| `DeepSeekClient` | 284 | class | live HTTP client |
+| `.__init__` | 293 | method | key/base URL/model/retry config |
+| `.close` | 324 | method | close internally owned httpx client |
+| `.__enter__` / `.__exit__` | 329/332 | methods | context manager |
+| `.complete` | 335 | method | POST + retry/backoff |
+| `FakeLLMClient` | 452 | class | scripted test client |
+| `.complete` | 488 | method | canned response or scripted error |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+MeteredLLMClient.complete(system, user):
+    try:
+        resp <- client.complete(system, user)
+    except Exception as exc:
+        calls += 1
+        attempts += getattr(exc, "attempts", 1)
+        retries += max(0, attempts_delta - 1)
+        retry_wait += getattr(exc, "retry_wait_s", 0)
+        failed_calls.append({attempts, retry_wait, error_type, message})
+        invoke_on_call()
+        raise
+    calls += 1
+    attempts += resp.attempts
+    retries += max(0, resp.attempts - 1)
+    latency += resp.latency_s; retry_wait += resp.retry_wait_s
+    token counters += resp fields
+    if resp.model_id: model_ids_seen.add(resp.model_id)
+    invoke_on_call()
+    return resp
+
+LLMSnapshot.__sub__(other):
+    return snapshot with every numeric field subtracted and
+    failed_parses = self.failed_parses[len(other.failed_parses):]
+
+resolve_model_alias(model=None):
+    return model or env("DEEPSEEK_MODEL") or "deepseek-flash"
+
+DeepSeekClient.complete(system, user):
+    build URL / headers / payload (model, system+user messages,
+        temperature=0.0, max_tokens=16, thinking={"type":"disabled"})
+    attempts <- 0; retry_wait <- 0; last_error <- None
+    while attempts <= max_retries:
+        attempts += 1
+        t0 <- now()
+        try:
+            resp <- http_client.post(url, json=payload, headers=headers)
+            latency <- now() - t0
+            if status == 200:
+                parse JSON; validate choices non-empty
+                extract content, prompt/completion/reasoning/cache tokens, model
+                return LLMResponse(..., attempts, retry_wait)
+            elif status in {429, 500, 502, 503, 504}:
+                last_error <- LLMTransportError(...)
+            else:
+                raise LLMTransportError(non-retryable)
+        except (TimeoutException, NetworkError) as e:
+            last_error <- e
+        except LLMTransportError:
+            raise
+        if attempts <= max_retries:
+            delay <- backoff[min(attempts-1, len(backoff)-1)]
+            sleep(delay); retry_wait += delay
+    raise LLMTransportError("failed after N attempts", attempts, retry_wait)
+
+FakeLLMClient.complete(system, user):
+    record (system, user) in call_history
+    if scripted errors: pop and raise
+    text <- responses(system,user) if callable
+            else dict lookup by (system,user) then user
+            else fixed str
+            else "NONE"
+    return LLMResponse(text, canned token counts, canned latency, model_id)
+```
+
+**Retry semantics.** Non-retryable 4xx raises immediately. Timeouts and
+network errors are retried. A 200 with invalid JSON or missing `choices` is
+retried. `attempts` in the final error includes the failed final attempt.
+
