+### 4.10 `src/graph_insertion/schedule.py`
+
+**Purpose:** refuse live runs that would overlap DeepSeek peak pricing
+([D-37]). Peak is Mon–Fri, 01:00–04:00 and 06:00–10:00 UTC.
+
+| Symbol | Line | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `_PEAK_WINDOWS` | 21 | `[(1,4), (6,10)]` |
+| `is_deepseek_peak` | 24 | weekday check + fractional-hour window check |
+| `window_intersects_peak` | 51 | sample start/end and every minute |
+| `format_peak_status` | 81 | human-readable UTC / PHT status |
+
+```
+is_deepseek_peak(dt):
+    if dt.weekday() >= 5: return False
+    h <- dt.hour + dt.minute/60
+    return any(start <= h < end for (start,end) in windows)
+
+window_intersects_peak(start, duration_s):
+    if duration_s < 0: ValueError
+    end <- start + duration_s
+    if is_peak(start) or is_peak(end): return True
+    for each whole minute strictly between start and end:
+        if is_peak(t): return True
+    return False
+
+format_peak_status(dt):
+    return formatted UTC time, UTC+8 time, and peak/off-peak status
+```
+
+**Conservative choice.** Chinese public holidays are not modelled; they are
+off-peak in reality, so the guard can over-report peak but never under-report.
