+### 4.11 `src/graph_insertion/scoring.py`
+
+**Purpose:** pure accuracy functions. Compares predicted edges and shortlist
+against the full gold graph and judgment set, with an explicit sensitivity
+variant for unjudged pairs ([D-30]).
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Kind | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `NodeScore` | 20 | frozen dataclass | per-held-out-node metrics |
+| `AggregateScore` | 83 | frozen dataclass | micro/macro + sensitivity aggregates |
+| `compute_gold_incident_edges` | 125 | function | all directed gold edges touching node |
+| `compute_gold_neighbours` | 135 | function | all distinct adjacent gold nodes |
+| `score_node_insertion` | 142 | function | score one trial |
+| `aggregate_scores` | 243 | function | micro + macro aggregation |
+
+**Pseudocode**
+
+```
+compute_gold_incident_edges(graph, node):
+    return {(p, node) for p in graph.prerequisites_of(node)}
+         | {(node, d) for d in graph.dependents_of(node)}
+
+compute_gold_neighbours(graph, node):
+    return set(graph.prerequisites_of(node)) | set(graph.dependents_of(node))
+
+score_node_insertion(node, gold_graph, judgments,
+                     shortlist_candidates, decided_edges):
+    gold_incident <- compute_gold_incident_edges(gold_graph, node)
+    gold_neighbours <- compute_gold_neighbours(gold_graph, node)
+    shortlist_set <- set(shortlist_candidates); decided_set <- set(decided_edges)
+
+    shortlist_hits <- |gold_neighbours ∩ shortlist_set|
+    shortlist_recall <- hits / |gold_neighbours|, or None if no neighbours
+
+    tp <- fp <- excluded <- 0
+    for (prereq, dep) in decided_set:
+        j_fwd <- judgments.judgment_for_edge(prereq, dep)
+        j_rev <- judgments.judgment_for_edge(dep, prereq)
+        if either is None:      excluded += 1        # unjudged direction
+        elif j_fwd is True:     tp += 1
+        else:                   fp += 1
+
+    fn <- |gold_incident \ decided_set|
+
+    precision <- tp/(tp+fp) if tp+fp > 0 else None
+    recall    <- tp/(tp+fn) if tp+fn > 0 else None
+    f1        <- 2tp/(2tp+fp+fn) if denominator > 0 else None
+
+    # sensitivity: unjudged predictions count as false positives
+    fp_sens <- fp + excluded
+    precision_sens <- tp/(tp+fp_sens) if denominator > 0 else None
+    recall_sens <- recall
+    f1_sens <- 2tp/(2tp+fp_sens+fn) if denominator > 0 else None
+    return NodeScore(...)
+
+aggregate_scores(node_scores):
+    if empty: return all zeros / None with zero defined-counts
+    totals <- sum every count across nodes
+    micro shortlist recall <- hits/gold_neighbours (1.0 if none)
+    micro precision <- tp/(tp+fp) (0.0 if none)
+    micro recall <- tp/(tp+fn) (1.0 if none)
+    micro f1 <- harmonic mean, 0.0 if both zero
+    macro metric <- mean of defined per-node values, or None
+    repeat micro/macro for sensitivity (fp_sens instead of fp)
+    return AggregateScore(...)
+```
+
+**Why both `j_forward` and `j_reverse` are checked.** A predicted edge is only
+counted as judged if neither ordered direction is missing from the file. If
+either is missing, the pair is set aside as `excluded_predictions`; the
+standard metric ignores it, while the sensitivity metric counts it as a false
+positive. This is the D-30 handling of the one missing DSA pair.
+
