+#### 4.13.4 `strategies/embedding_threshold.py`
+
+| Symbol | Line | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `DEFAULT_THETA` | 59 | `0.6` |
+| `EmbeddingThresholdStrategy` | 62 | Strategy 2 |
+| `.__init__` | 80 | validate `theta` in `[-1,1]` |
+| `.setup` | 106 | batch embed all nodes, L2-normalise, preallocate matrix |
+| `.shortlist` | 176 | embed query once, cosine > theta, sort |
+| `.on_inserted` | 267 | append cached vector; capacity doubling |
+| `.config` | 309 | `{theta, seed}` |
+| `.diagnostics` | 313 | comparisons/threshold/size/max cosine/index size |
+
+**Internal state:** `_mat` is a row-major `float32` matrix of L2-normalised
+vectors with capacity `max(16, 2n)` initially. `_names[i]` is the name at row
+`i`; `_name_to_idx` maps names to rows; `_n` is the number of live rows.
+
+```
+setup(graph, embedder):
+    reset all state to not-set-up
+    nodes <- sorted(graph.nodes()); n <- len(nodes)
+    if n == 0: mark set-up; return
+    raw <- embedder.embed_many([embed_text(node) for node in nodes])
+    require 2-D, n rows, all finite
+    norms <- row norms; require every norm > 0
+    normed <- raw / norms[:, None] as float32
+    capacity <- max(16, 2n)
+    _mat <- zeros((capacity, dim)); _mat[:n] <- normed
+    _names <- nodes; _name_to_idx <- {name: i}
+    _n <- n; _embedder <- embedder; mark set-up
+
+shortlist(new_name):
+    clear cache and failure state first
+    require set-up; validate(new_name)
+    raw <- embedder.embed(embed_text(new_name))       # exactly one call
+    require 1-D, finite, norm > 0; check/establish dim
+    q <- raw / ||raw||
+    cache (new_name, q)
+    if _n == 0: return empty
+    scores <- _mat[:_n] @ q
+    max_cos <- max(scores); comparisons <- _n
+    mask <- float64(scores) > theta                   # strict >
+    qualifying <- indices where mask
+    items <- [(score, name) for qualifying indices if name != new_name]
+    sort items by (-score, name)
+    return Shortlist(names, scores)
+
+on_inserted(new_name, edges):
+    require cache matches new_name and vec exists
+    require new_name not already indexed
+    vec <- cached; clear cache
+    if capacity full: double capacity and copy
+    _mat[_n] <- vec; _name_to_idx[new_name] <- _n
+    _names.append(new_name); _n += 1
+```
+
+**Semantics.** Strict `>` threshold; zero-candidate shortlists are expected
+and valid. Scores are float32, so a cosine may exceed 1.0 by rounding error.
+`diagnostics()["max_cosine"]` is over the whole index, including a row for
+`new_name` only if it was already indexed — unreachable through `insert_node`.
+
+#### 4.13.5 `strategies/ann_retrieval.py`
+
+| Symbol | Line | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `AnnRetrievalStrategy` | 83 | Strategy 3, FAISS HNSW |
+| `.__init__` | 108 | validate `k`, `M`, `ef_construction`, `ef_search`; require faiss |
+| `.max_candidates` | 161 | `min(k, n)` |
+| `.setup` | 168 | batch embed, normalise, single-threaded HNSW build |
+| `.shortlist` | 250 | embed query once, HNSW search, filter/pad, sort |
+| `.on_inserted` | 368 | add cached vector to HNSW index |
+| `.config` | 403 | all HNSW parameters + faiss identity |
+| `.diagnostics` | 417 | index size, max cosine, exact-top-k overlap |
+
+**Index:** `faiss.IndexHNSWFlat(dim, M, METRIC_INNER_PRODUCT)` over
+L2-normalised `float32` vectors. Inner product on unit vectors equals cosine
+similarity. `setup` calls `faiss.omp_set_num_threads(1)` before the batch add.
+
+```
+setup(graph, embedder):
+    reset state
+    nodes <- sorted(graph.nodes()); n <- len(nodes)
+    if n == 0: mark set-up; return
+    raw <- embedder.embed_many(texts)
+    validate 2-D, n rows, finite, positive norms, dim > 0
+    normed <- contiguous float32(raw / norms[:, None])
+    faiss.omp_set_num_threads(1)
+    index <- IndexHNSWFlat(dim, M, INNER_PRODUCT)
+    index.hnsw.efConstruction <- ef_construction
+    index.hnsw.efSearch <- ef_search
+    index.add(normed)
+    store dim/index/names/map; set-up
+
+shortlist(new_name):
+    clear per-query cache and diagnostic state first
+    require set-up; validate(new_name)
+    raw <- embedder.embed(embed_text(new_name))       # exactly one call
+    validate 1-D, finite, positive norm, dimension
+    if dim unknown: lazily create HNSW index
+    q <- contiguous float32(raw / ||raw||)
+    cache (new_name, q); record n_at_query, query name/vector
+    if index empty: return empty
+    index.hnsw.efSearch <- ef_search
+    k_eff <- min(k + (1 if new_name already indexed else 0), n_indexed)
+    distances, labels <- index.search(q.reshape(1,-1), k_eff)
+    for (dist, label):
+        if label == -1: continue
+        name <- _names[label]
+        if name == new_name or seen: continue
+        append (name, dist)
+    sort by (-score, name); take first k
+    record shortlist, max valid distance, returned candidates
+    return Shortlist(names, scores)
+
+on_inserted(new_name, edges):
+    require cached name matches and vector exists
+    require new_name not already in map
+    vec <- cached; clear cache
+    index.add(vec.reshape(1,-1))
+    append name; map name -> len(names)-1
+```
+
+**Diagnostics.** `exact_topk_overlap` is computed in `diagnostics()`, outside
+all timed windows, by reconstructing the first `n_at_query` vectors with
+`index.reconstruct_n` and comparing the exact top-k cosine set with what HNSW
+returned. This measures approximation fidelity, not shortlist cost.
+
+#### 4.13.6 `strategies/bounded_bucket.py`
+
+**Purpose:** Strategy 4. Nodes are ordered by inverse reflected-Gray rank of
+their random-hyperplane LSH code. That order is partitioned into contiguous
+segments of size at most `s_max` (and at least `s_min` after setup where
+possible). A query only touches the home segment. Segment overflow splits at
+the midpoint; setup merges undersize segments.
+
+**Symbol map**
+
+| Symbol | Line | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `DEFAULT_S_MIN` / `S_MAX` / `N_BITS` / `SEED` | 78–81 | `5`, `10`, `12`, `42` |
+| `BucketEntry` | 84 | frozen `(gray, name, code, row)`; sort key `(gray, name)` |
+| `BoundedBucketStrategy` | 98 | Strategy 4 |
+| `.__init__` | 123 | validate bounds; `s_max >= 2*s_min`, `1 <= n_bits <= 62` |
+| `.max_candidates` | 192 | `min(s_max, n)` |
+| `._draw_hyperplanes` | 199 | deterministic unit-normal matrix from seed |
+| `._gray_rank` | 212 | inverse reflected Gray code via prefix XOR |
+| `._hamming` | 221 | integer XOR popcount |
+| `._hash_vector` | 225 | float64 projection -> `(code, gray)` |
+| `._hash_matrix` | 237 | vectorised projection -> code/gray lists |
+| `._bisect_recursive` | 250 | split list until each piece <= `s_max` |
+| `._choose_neighbour` | 262 | proximity tuple chooses left/right |
+| `._locate_home` | 290 | binary search segment last-keys, return `(index, inside_span)` |
+| `._insert_entry` | 331 | sorted insertion; split if overflow |
+| `.setup` | 368 | batch build segments from initial graph |
+| `.shortlist` | 532 | hash query, locate home segment, score members |
+| `.on_inserted` | 667 | cache checks, matrix append, segment insert/split |
+| `._compute_exact_topk_overlap` | 729 | exact top-m overlap for diagnostics |
+| `.config` | 759 | `{s_min, s_max, n_bits, seed}` |
+| `.diagnostics` | 768 | bucket/segment/query details |
+
+**Pseudocode: hashing helpers**
+
+```
+_draw_hyperplanes(dim):
+    rng <- default_rng(seed)
+    raw <- rng.standard_normal((n_bits, dim), float64)
+    normalise rows (zero norm -> 1); return float64
+
+_gray_rank(code):
+    g <- code; shift <- 1
+    while shift < n_bits:
+        g ^= g >> shift; shift <<= 1
+    return g
+
+_hamming(a, b): return bit_count(a XOR b)
+
+_hash_vector(vec):
+    dots <- float64(vec) @ hyperplanes.T
+    code <- 0
+    for r in 0..n_bits-1:
+        bit <- 1 if dots[r] >= 0 else 0
+        code |= bit << (n_bits - 1 - r)
+    return code, _gray_rank(code)
+
+_hash_matrix(mat):
+    dots <- float64(mat) @ hyperplanes.T
+    codes <- vectorised sign bits as above
+    return codes, [_gray_rank(c) for c in codes]
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: ordering and neighbour choice**
+
+```
+_bisect_recursive(entries, s_max):
+    if len(entries) <= s_max: return [entries]
+    mid <- len(entries) // 2
+    return _bisect_recursive(entries[:mid], s_max)
+         + _bisect_recursive(entries[mid:], s_max)
+
+_choose_neighbour(left, right, cur_first_code, cur_first_gray,
+                  cur_last_code, cur_last_gray):
+    if left is None: return "right"
+    if right is None: return "left"
+    left_key  <- (hamming(left[-1].code, cur_first_code),
+                  cur_first_gray - left[-1].gray,
+                  len(left), 0)
+    right_key <- (hamming(cur_last_code, right[0].code),
+                  right[0].gray - cur_last_gray,
+                  len(right), 1)
+    return "left" if left_key <= right_key else "right"
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: home lookup**
+
+```
+_locate_home(gray, name, code):
+    require segments non-empty
+    key <- (gray, name)
+    binary search first segment whose last sort key >= key -> pos
+    if pos valid and segment[pos].first <= key <= segment[pos].last:
+        return pos, True
+    if pos == 0: return 0, False
+    if pos == len(segments): return len(segments)-1, False
+    side <- _choose_neighbour(segments[pos-1], segments[pos],
+                              code, gray, code, gray)
+    return (pos-1 if side == "left" else pos), False
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: insertion**
+
+```
+_insert_entry(entry):
+    prior_n <- self._n - 1
+    if no segments: segments <- [[entry]]; sizes/flags <- 1/False/False; return
+    home_idx, inside_span <- _locate_home(entry.gray, entry.name, entry.code)
+    merge_occurred <- (not inside_span) and prior_n >= 1
+    seg <- segments[home_idx]
+    ins_pos <- first index where seg[i].sort_key() >= entry.sort_key()
+    seg.insert(ins_pos, entry)
+    if len(seg) > s_max:
+        mid <- len(seg) // 2
+        segments[home_idx:home_idx+1] <- [seg[:mid], seg[mid:]]
+        split_occurred <- True
+        bucket_size <- len(left_half) if ins_pos < mid else len(right_half)
+    else:
+        split_occurred <- False; bucket_size <- len(seg)
+    merge_occurred flag recorded
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: setup**
+
+```
+setup(graph, embedder):
+    reset state
+    nodes <- sorted(graph.nodes()); n <- len(nodes)
+    if n == 0: mark set-up; return
+    raw <- embedder.embed_many(texts)
+    validate 2-D, n rows, finite, positive norms, dim > 0
+    normed <- float32(raw / norms[:, None])
+    hyperplanes <- _draw_hyperplanes(dim)
+    codes, grays <- _hash_matrix(normed)
+    entries <- [BucketEntry(gray[i], nodes[i], code[i], row=i)]
+    entry_by_name <- map by name
+    sort entries by (gray, name)
+
+    if n < s_min:
+        segments <- [entries]
+    else:
+        group consecutive entries with identical gray into raw buckets
+        segments <- concat(_bisect_recursive(bucket, s_max) for bucket in buckets)
+        i <- 0
+        while i < len(segments) and len(segments) > 1:
+            if len(segments[i]) < s_min:
+                choose left/right neighbour via proximity tuple
+                combine the two adjacent segments
+                if combined size <= s_max:
+                    replace both with one segment
+                else:
+                    replace both with two halves at len//2
+                i <- max(0, left_index)      # re-check merged region
+            else: i += 1
+
+    _mat <- zeros((max(16, 2n), dim)); _mat[:n] <- normed
+    store dim/mat/names/map/entries/segments/n; set-up
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: shortlist**
+
+```
+shortlist(new_name):
+    clear caches and per-query diagnostics first
+    require set-up; validate(new_name)
+    raw <- embedder.embed(embed_text(new_name))       # exactly one call
+    validate 1-D, finite, positive norm, dimension
+    if dim unknown: set dim, draw hyperplanes, allocate matrix
+    q <- contiguous float32(raw / ||raw||)
+    code, gray <- _hash_vector(q)
+    cache q/code/gray; record query diagnostics
+    if _n == 0: return empty
+    home_idx, inside_span <- _locate_home(gray, new_name, code)
+    seg <- segments[home_idx]
+    record bucket id, gray range, inside-span, sizes, whether code exists
+    filtered <- [e for e in seg if e.name != new_name]
+    if empty: return empty
+    scores <- _mat[[e.row for e in filtered]] @ q
+    paired <- [(score, name, code)]
+    sort by (-score, name)
+    return Shortlist(names, scores)                   # all members, <= s_max
+```
+
+**Pseudocode: update and diagnostics**
+
+```
+on_inserted(new_name, edges):
+    require cached name/vector/code/gray all match new_name
+    require new_name not already indexed
+    consume cache
+    if matrix full: double capacity and copy
+    row <- _n
+    _mat[row] <- vec; names.append; map[name] <- row; _n += 1
+    entry <- BucketEntry(gray, name, code, row)
+    entry_by_name[name] <- entry
+    _insert_entry(entry)
+
+_compute_exact_topk_overlap():
+    if shortlist never called or no query vector: return None
+    if n_at_query == 0: return 1.0
+    cosines <- _mat[:n_at_query] @ query
+    valid <- rows whose name != query_name
+    sort by (-cosine, name); m <- min(s_max, len(valid))
+    exact_set <- first m names
+    matched <- returned candidates in exact_set
+    return matched / m
+```
+
+**Why the Gray order.** Adjacent Gray codes differ by one bit, so ordering by
+inverse Gray rank keeps nearby LSH codes physically adjacent in the segment
+list. The home segment is therefore approximately a locality-preserving
+interval of embedding space. `exact_topk_overlap` measures the combined loss
+from partitioning and embedding approximation.
+
