+## 5. Analysis pipeline (Phase 4)
+
+This section is an outline plus pseudocode for the dataflow-critical
+functions. Plotting functions share a common pattern: filter to primary
+variants, read precomputed table rows, draw, write `.pdf`, `.png`, and a
+figure CSV. They are listed by contract rather than reproduced line by line.
+
+### 5.1 `scripts/analysis/validate_runs.py`
+
+**Purpose:** fail-closed gate. No table or figure is produced from data that
+has not passed it. Implements the Phase 4 analysis plan, Section 2.
+
+**Checks**
+
+1. Exact trial counts: accuracy 59 total (29 DSA + 30 Metacademy), sweep 60
+   (10 per size), legacy DSA-only 29.
+2. Planned call bound keyed by sidecar strategy and config; directory name
+   must match manifest `run_id` and canonical sidecar slug.
+3. Independent recomputation of summary metrics from `raw.jsonl`:
+   micro/macro P/R/F1, shortlist recall, mean/median total time, mean/sum
+   calls, integer summary fields.
+4. Manifest/provenance: `git_dirty` false; commit uniform within mode; across
+   modes allowed only with `--src-diff-clean`; all 7 required libraries
+   present and uniform.
+5. Embedder identity and thread pin: embedding strategies must record
+   `cpu_threads == 1`, `torch_threads == 1`, model name and revision;
+   brute force must have no active embedding model or thread pin.
+6. Resume detection: duplicate keys where an earlier record succeeded are
+   corrupt; failed-then-succeeded keys are valid and reported.
+7. Optional external sha256 hashes for the four artifacts.
+8. Table T3 inventory with per-file and composite directory hashes.
+
