+### 5.5 `scripts/analysis/stats.py`
+
+| Symbol | Line | Contract |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `classify_slope_flatness` | 25 | D2 bins: `<0.1` flat, `0.1–0.9` sub-linear, `>0.9` linear; NaN -> undefined |
+| `fit_log_log_slope` | 37 | OLS of `log(mean_cost)` on `log(n)`; undefined on non-positive/non-finite |
+| `bootstrap_slope_ci` | 80 | resample trials within each size; drop zero-mean resamples; report `n_boot_used` |
+| `evaluate_dominance` | 157 | R2 mechanical dominance with 0.025 F1 tolerance |
+
+```
+fit_log_log_slope(sizes, means):
+    if <2 points, length mismatch, any size <= 0/non-finite,
+       any mean <= 0/non-finite: return (NaN, NaN, NaN)
+    x <- log(sizes); y <- log(means)
+    slope <- sum((x-xbar)(y-ybar)) / sum((x-xbar)^2)
+    intercept <- ybar - slope*xbar
+    r2 <- correlation^2 (1.0 if y variance zero)
+    return slope, intercept, r2
+
+bootstrap_slope_ci(size_to_trials):
+    if <2 sizes: undefined
+    if any size has no trials: undefined, category names sizes
+    empirical means; if any <=0/non-finite: undefined, category names sizes
+    point slope <- fit_log_log_slope(sizes, empirical means)
+    for n_resamples:
+        for each size: resample trials with replacement; mean
+        if any resample mean <=0/non-finite: discard whole resample
+        fit slope on log(resample means) vs log(size)
+    CI <- percentile 2.5/97.5 of valid slopes
+    return point, low, high, category, r2, n_boot_used
+
+evaluate_dominance(a, b, threshold=0.025):
+    if |f1_a - f1_b| < threshold: return "not distinguishable"
+    if f1_a > f1_b and calls_a <= calls_b: return "A dominates B"
+    if f1_b > f1_a and calls_b <= calls_a: return "B dominates A"
+    return "trade-off"
+```
