+### 5.7 `scripts/analysis/posthoc.py`
+
+**Purpose:** post-hoc decision and ranking stage (Tables T5–T9b, Figures
+F7–F9). Explicitly marked `POST HOC: not pre-registered` in every output. No
+live calls; consumes T1/T2 aggregates and raw accuracy runs.
+
+**Core concepts**
+
+- Strategies: brute force, embedding threshold, ANN, bounded bucket, in
+  frozen order.
+- Corpora: DSA, Metacademy.
+- `A_i`: min-max normalised mean F1 (higher is better).
+- `C_i`: min-max normalised `log10(1 + mean calls)` (lower is better).
+- `w` scenarios: fixed weights across the cost/accuracy trade-off.
+- Gates: G1 relative accuracy, G2 call cap at `n=2000`, G3 non-dominance.
+- Rankings: weighted sum, TOPSIS, Kendall tau-b, Monte Carlo rank shares,
+  analytic rank shares, wall-clock-substituted sensitivity.
+
