+## 6. Supporting tooling (not core runtime)
+
+### 6.1 `scripts/generate_name_pool.py` (~2,400 lines)
+
+Generates the synthetic concept-name pool (`data/synthetic/cs_concept_names.json`)
+used by the sweep. Two backends: direct DeepSeek API, or an external command
+adapter. Supports sharding, cache/resume, deduplication, corpus-overlap
+validation, and a `--verify` mode.
+
+**High-level flow**
+
+```
+parse args
+  -> choose backend (DeepSeek or command adapter)
+  -> determine shard (subfield subset) if --shard I/N
+  -> load cache for (run_id, shard)
+  -> for each round and subfield:
+        build prompt asking for new snake_case CS concept names
+        call backend
+        parse JSON array
+        validate snake_case, dedupe, reject corpus overlap
+        append accepted names to cache and pool
+        stop when target reached or max calls
+  -> optionally merge shards into one pool
+  -> optionally verify pool against benchmark corpora
+```
+
+**Key symbols:** `ShardLockManager`, `CacheEntry`, `load_completed_cache`,
+`append_cache_record`, `load_benchmark_corpus_concepts`,
+`validate_and_dedupe_candidates`, `build_pool_from_cache`, `verify_pool`,
+`GenerationBackend`, `DeepSeekGenerationBackend`, `CommandGenerationBackend`,
+`run_generation_loop`, `main`.
+
+### 6.2 `scripts/name_pool_supervisor.py` (~1,300 lines)
+
+Runs multiple shard subprocesses unattended. Rotates rate-limited or busy
+profiles onto spare profiles, tracks cooldowns, writes atomic status JSON and
+a JSONL supervisor log, handles SIGINT/SIGTERM by terminating the descendant
+process tree, and automatically builds and verifies the merged pool when all
+shards finish.
+
+**Exit codes:** generator `0` ok, `1` error, `2` usage, `3` rate limit,
+`4` login required, `5` model mismatch, `6` consecutive failures, `7` profile
+in use. Supervisor `0` ok, `1` error, `2` usage, `3` stalled, `4` max total
+calls, `130` signal.
